---
import Entry from '../../../layouts/Entry.astro';
import { url } from '../../../lib/site';
import manifest from '../../../../public/data/funding-flows/us-schedule-i/manifest.json';
import filingContext from '../../../../public/data/funding-flows/us-schedule-i/filing-context.json';
import '../../../styles/charity-financial-search.css';

const title = 'Grants reported on U.S. Form 990 Schedule I';
const count = (value: number) => value.toLocaleString('en-US');
const base = '/data/funding-flows/us-schedule-i/';
const instructions = 'https://www.irs.gov/instructions/i990si';
const sources = [
  { title: 'Form 990 electronic filing archive', publisher: manifest.source.publisher, url: 'https://www.irs.gov/charities-non-profits/form-990-series-downloads' },
  { title: 'Schedule I instructions', publisher: manifest.source.publisher, url: instructions },
];
---

<Entry title={title} eyebrow="The Record · Funding flows" summary="Follow cash grants and noncash assistance reported by U.S. organizations, with original filing coordinates and exact recipient EINs." crumbs={[{label:'The Record',href:'/record/'},{label:'Global Charity Index',href:'/record/charity-index/'},{label:'Schedule I grants'}]} sources={sources}>
  <p>This edition links {count(manifest.counts.includedRows)} reported grant rows from {count(manifest.counts.includedFilings)} original Form 990 filings to dated IRS identities for the filer and the named recipient. It covers one IRS archive labeled January 2024 and selected tax periods ending in 2022 or 2023.</p>
  <section class="charity-financial-search" data-us-grants data-manifest={JSON.stringify(manifest)} data-file={url(base + manifest.asset.path)} data-finances={url('/record/charity-financials/united-states/')} aria-labelledby="us-grants-heading">
    <h2 id="us-grants-heading">Find grants by EIN</h2>
    <p id="us-grants-hint">Enter an Employer Identification Number (EIN) to find records where it appears as the filer or recipient. The lookup stays in this browser. <a href={url('/record/charity-index/')}>Find an EIN by name</a>.</p>
    <form aria-describedby="us-grants-hint">
      <label for="us-grants-query">Employer Identification Number</label>
      <div class="finance-actions">
        <input id="us-grants-query" name="q" type="search" maxlength="10" autocomplete="off" disabled />
        <button class="btn" type="submit" disabled>Search grants</button>
        <button class="btn btn-ghost" type="button" data-clear disabled>Clear</button>
      </div>
      <label class="version-filter"><input type="checkbox" data-include-competing disabled /> Include rows from filings with another published version</label>
    </form>
    <p role="status" data-status>Search when you’re ready to load the public records.</p>
    <div class="finance-actions">
      <button class="btn btn-ghost btn-small" type="button" data-json disabled>Export all matches as JSON</button>
      <button class="btn btn-ghost btn-small" type="button" data-csv disabled>Export all matches as CSV</button>
    </div>
    <ol class="finance-results" data-site-symbol="gift" aria-label="United States Schedule I grants" data-results></ol>
    <noscript><p>For the original source without JavaScript, use the IRS archive below.</p></noscript>
  </section>
  <h2 id="coverage">Coverage and original records</h2>
  <p><a href={instructions}>Schedule I Part II</a> asks for domestic organizations or governments that received more than $5,000 from the filer during the tax year. Each source row reports a filer-recipient amount for a period. The noncash value uses the filer’s reported valuation. The source gives no dates for individual payments and the recipient’s own spending requires other evidence.</p>
  <p>Both EINs must match the dated IRS identity snapshot. The edition leaves out unresolved and self-recipient rows, repeated recipient lines within one return, and otherwise eligible rows from competing filings in this archive. A filing outside this archive may change the picture. The edition never adds the cash and noncash figures into one total.</p>
  <p>Charitology checked the IRS indexes published for 2022–2026 against the original XML. The check found {count(filingContext.counts.alternateFilingObjects)} other filing objects with the same filer EIN and exact tax-period start and end dates as {count(filingContext.counts.filingsWithAnotherVersion)} of the January filings. {count(filingContext.counts.alternateObjectsWithDifferentRecordedPartII)} of those other objects record different Part II recipient identifiers or amounts. By default, search excludes the {count(filingContext.counts.rowsFromFilingsWithAnotherVersion)} rows affected. The optional results link the other filing objects. The IRS files supply the reported values. Selecting an authoritative version requires further evidence.</p>
  <p>Of {count(manifest.counts.partIIOrganizationRows)} source rows, {count(manifest.counts.includedRows)} are included. The source manifest gives the count for each exclusion. The full-form finance links look up the same EIN in a separate extract edition. An available period can add financial context for that organization.</p>
  <p><a href={manifest.source.archive}>Original IRS ZIP</a> · <a href={url(base + 'manifest.json')}>Source and coverage manifest</a> · <a href={url(base + manifest.asset.path)}>Full selected snapshot as compressed JSON</a> · <a href={url(base + 'filing-context.json')}>Filing version references and fingerprints</a>. Import EINs and filing object numbers as text.</p>
</Entry>

<style>
  .version-filter { display: flex; align-items: flex-start; gap: .5rem; margin-top: .8rem; }
  .version-filter input { flex: none; margin: .35rem 0 0; padding: 0; }
</style>

<script>
  import { $, h } from '../../../lib/client/dom';
  import { download, toCsv } from '../../../lib/client/files';
  import { loadVerifiedJson } from '../../../lib/client/verified-json';
  import { normalizeEin } from '../../../lib/irs-registry.mjs';
  import filingContext from '../../../../public/data/funding-flows/us-schedule-i/filing-context.json';

  type Grant = [string, number, number | null, number | null];
  type Filing = [string, string, string, string, Grant[]];
  type Snapshot = { filings: Filing[]; filingSha256: Record<string, string> };
  type Manifest = typeof import('../../../../public/data/funding-flows/us-schedule-i/manifest.json');
  type Match = { filerEin: string; recipientEin: string; taxPeriodStart: string; taxPeriodEnd: string; filingObjectId: string;
    partIIRow: number; cashGrantUSD: number | null; nonCashAssistanceUSD: number | null; filingSha256: string };
  const dollars = new Intl.NumberFormat('en-US', { style: 'currency', currency: 'USD', maximumFractionDigits: 0 });
  const money = (amount: number | null) => amount === null ? 'Not supplied' : dollars.format(amount);
  const formattedEin = (ein: string) => `${ein.slice(0, 2)}-${ein.slice(2)}`;
  const otherVersions = new Map(filingContext.filings.map(row => [row.filingObjectId, row.alternatives]));

  for (const root of document.querySelectorAll<HTMLElement>('[data-us-grants]')) {
    const manifest: Manifest = JSON.parse(root.dataset.manifest!);
    const form = $<HTMLFormElement>('form', root);
    const input = $<HTMLInputElement>('input[type=search]', form);
    const includeCompeting = $<HTMLInputElement>('[data-include-competing]', form);
    const submit = $<HTMLButtonElement>('button[type=submit]', form);
    const clear = $<HTMLButtonElement>('[data-clear]', root);
    const status = $('[data-status]', root);
    const results = $('[data-results]', root);
    const json = $<HTMLButtonElement>('[data-json]', root);
    const csv = $<HTMLButtonElement>('[data-csv]', root);
    let loaded: Promise<Snapshot> | undefined;
    let matches: Match[] = [];
    let sequence = 0;
    let omitted = 0;
    const prefilled = new URLSearchParams(location.hash.slice(1)).get('ein');
    if (prefilled && /^(?:[0-9]{9}|[0-9]{2}-[0-9]{7})$/.test(prefilled)) input.value = prefilled;
    input.disabled = submit.disabled = clear.disabled = includeCompeting.disabled = false;

    async function load() {
      const data = await loadVerifiedJson(root.dataset.file!, manifest.asset) as Snapshot;
      if (!Array.isArray(data?.filings) || data.filings.length !== manifest.asset.rows) throw new Error('The Schedule I edition has an unexpected filing count.');
      return data;
    }

    function reset() {
      matches = [];
      omitted = 0;
      results.replaceChildren();
      json.disabled = csv.disabled = true;
    }

    function financeLink(ein: string) {
      return h('a', { href: root.dataset.finances! + '#ein=' + ein }, `EIN ${formattedEin(ein)}`);
    }

    function display(row: Match) {
      const alternatives = otherVersions.get(row.filingObjectId);
      return h('li', { class: 'card' },
        h('h3', {}, 'Reported grant to ', financeLink(row.recipientEin)),
        h('p', {}, 'Filer ', financeLink(row.filerEin), ` · Tax period ${row.taxPeriodStart} to ${row.taxPeriodEnd}`),
        h('p', {}, `Cash grant ${money(row.cashGrantUSD)} · Noncash assistance ${money(row.nonCashAssistanceUSD)}`),
        h('p', { class: 'note' }, h('a', { href: manifest.source.archive }, 'IRS archive'),
          ` · Filing object ${row.filingObjectId} · Schedule I Part II row ${row.partIIRow}`),
        alternatives ? h('details', {}, h('summary', {}, 'Other filing objects for this exact tax period'),
          h('ul', {}, alternatives.map(alternate => h('li', {},
            h('a', { href: alternate.archive }, 'IRS archive'), ` · Filing object ${alternate.filingObjectId} · `,
            alternate.sameRecordedPartIIAmountsAndRecipientIdentifiers ? 'Same recorded Part II identifiers and amounts' : 'Different recorded Part II identifiers or amounts')))) : null);
    }

    form.addEventListener('submit', async event => {
      event.preventDefault();
      const ticket = ++sequence;
      reset();
      try {
        const ein = normalizeEin(input.value);
        const include = includeCompeting.checked;
        submit.disabled = true;
        status.textContent = 'Checking the public Schedule I records.';
        loaded ??= load().catch(error => { loaded = undefined; throw error; });
        const { filings, filingSha256 } = await loaded;
        if (ticket !== sequence) return;
        for (const [filerEin, taxPeriodStart, taxPeriodEnd, filingObjectId, grants] of filings) {
          for (const [recipientEin, partIIRow, cashGrantUSD, nonCashAssistanceUSD] of grants) {
            if (filerEin !== ein && recipientEin !== ein) continue;
            if (!include && otherVersions.has(filingObjectId)) {
              omitted++;
              continue;
            }
            matches.push({ filerEin, recipientEin, taxPeriodStart, taxPeriodEnd, filingObjectId, partIIRow, cashGrantUSD, nonCashAssistanceUSD, filingSha256: filingSha256[filingObjectId] });
          }
        }
        matches.sort((a, b) => b.taxPeriodEnd.localeCompare(a.taxPeriodEnd) || a.filingObjectId.localeCompare(b.filingObjectId) || a.partIIRow - b.partIIRow);
        const displayed = matches.slice(0, 40);
        const found = matches.length ? `${matches.length} ${matches.length === 1 ? 'record' : 'records'}. Showing ${displayed.length}.` : 'No matching grant rows in this search.';
        status.textContent = found + (omitted ? ` ${omitted} ${omitted === 1 ? 'row' : 'rows'} from filings with another version left out.` : '');
        results.append(...displayed.map(display));
        json.disabled = csv.disabled = matches.length === 0;
      } catch (error) {
        if (ticket === sequence) status.textContent = error instanceof Error ? error.message : 'The grant search failed.';
      } finally { if (ticket === sequence) submit.disabled = false; }
    });

    includeCompeting.addEventListener('change', () => {
      if (input.value.trim()) form.requestSubmit();
    });

    clear.addEventListener('click', () => {
      sequence++;
      reset();
      input.value = '';
      includeCompeting.checked = false;
      submit.disabled = false;
      status.textContent = 'Search cleared.';
      input.focus();
    });

    const { source, registry, currency, capturedOn } = manifest;
    json.addEventListener('click', () => {
      if (!matches.length) return;
      const included = new Set(matches.map(row => row.filingObjectId));
      const filingVersions = { checkedOn: filingContext.capturedOn, scope: filingContext.scope, omittedGrantRows: omitted,
        alternatives: filingContext.filings.filter(row => included.has(row.filingObjectId)) };
      download('us-schedule-i-grants.json', JSON.stringify({ source, registry, currency, capturedOn, grants: matches, filingVersions }, null, 2) + '\n', 'application/json');
    });
    csv.addEventListener('click', () => {
      if (!matches.length) return;
      const rows = matches.map(row => ({ ...row, currency, capturedOn, registryDate: registry.date, registrySha256: registry.manifestSha256,
        source: source.archive, sourceSha256: source.sha256, publisher: source.publisher, scope: source.scope,
        alternateFilingCount: otherVersions.get(row.filingObjectId)?.length ?? 0, filingVersionsCheckedOn: filingContext.capturedOn }));
      download('us-schedule-i-grants.csv', '\uFEFF' + toCsv(rows), 'text/csv;charset=utf-8');
    });
  }
</script>
